-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"GA"},{"bioguideId":"W000817","fullName":"Sen. Warren, Elizabeth [D-MA]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MA"},{"bioguideId":"W000800","fullName":"Sen. Welch, Peter [D-VT]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VT"},{"bioguideId":"W000802","fullName":"Sen. Whitehouse, Sheldon [D-RI]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"RI"},{"bioguideId":"W000779","fullName":"Sen. Wyden, Ron [D-OR]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OR"},{"bioguideId":"H001089","fullName":"Sen. Hawley, Josh [R-MO]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-07","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MO"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-17T07:28:59+00:00","id":"s3071-119","introducedDate":"2025-10-29","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-10-29","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Appropriations."},"laws":[],"number":"3071","originChamber":"Senate","policyArea":"Agriculture and Food","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"L000570","district":null,"fullName":"Sen. Luján, Ben Ray [D-NM]","party":"D","state":"NM"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-10-29","actionDesc":"Introduced in Senate","text":"<p><strong>Keep SNAP and WIC Funded Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill provides FY2026 appropriations for the Department of Agriculture (USDA) to continue operating the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP); the Special Supplemental Nutrition Program for Women, Infants, and Children (WIC); and a related block grant program if there is a lapse in FY2026 appropriations for USDA.</p><p>Specifically, the bill provides appropriations to USDA for any period in which legislation to provide FY2026 interim continuing appropriations or full-year appropriations for USDA has not been enacted. If such a lapse in appropriations occurs, the bill provides the appropriations that are necessary to continue</p><ul><li>providing uninterrupted SNAP benefits,</li><li>providing consolidated block grants to Puerto Rico and American Samoa for nutrition assistance programs, and</li><li>carrying out&nbsp;WIC without interruption.</li></ul><p>In addition, the bill provides appropriations to pay any benefits under these programs that were missed on or after September 30, 2025, and before this bill is enacted.</p><p>The appropriations for these purposes are available until the earlier of (1) the&nbsp;enactment into law of legislation to provide FY2026 appropriations for USDA (including continuing appropriations), or (2) September 30, 2026.&nbsp;</p><p>The bill also requires USDA to use the funds provided by this bill to reimburse state agencies for costs that were incurred to carry out these programs during a lapse in appropriations, to the extent that the programs were carried out in accordance with federal law (including regulations) during the lapse.&nbsp;</p>","updateDate":"2025-11-06T11:49:40Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Keep SNAP and WIC Funded Act of 2025","type":"s","updateDate":"2025-12-05T21:59:58Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2025-12-05T21:59:58Z"}
